You can absolutely do that. However, since you've decided on a single-page website, you don't actually need a router that loads separate HTML pages.

I'd recommend building a very lightweight hash-based router. It will give you URLs like:
localhost:5500/#/
localhost:5500/#/osnovi
localhost:5500/#/nivелир
localhost:5500/#/visinski-sistemi
localhost:5500/#/reperi


The navbar stays in place, and JavaScript switches the content inside the main container.
